f(11,'workedExample','The hybrid share combines an ML-KEM-768 encapsulation key (1,184 bytes) and X25519 share (32 bytes): 1,216 bytes. Both shared secrets enter the key schedule. The design protects recorded traffic if a component remains secure under the combiner assumptions. It neither upgrades certificate signatures nor replaces record AEAD; quantum-capable active attackers would require resistant authentication too.')
